import time

class GreenSkillsPortal:
    def __init__(self):
        self.regional_db = {
            "balaghat": {
                "district_name": "Balaghat, MP",
                "partner_industries": ["MOIL (Manganese Ore India Ltd)", "HCL (Hindustan Copper Ltd)"],
                "available_tasks": [{"task_id": 101, "name": "Eco-furniture making from bamboo waste", "base_credits": 50}]
            }
        }
        self.user_wallet = {"name": "Ramlal Baiga", "location": "Balaghat", "earned_credits": 0}

    def simulate_submission(self, task_id, latitude, longitude):
        print(f"\n🚀 [MY BHARAT] New submission received | Lat {latitude}, Long {longitude}")
        time.sleep(1)
        
        # Module 1: AI Verification
        print("🔍 [AI VERIFICATION] Checking the uploaded photo...")
        print("✅ AI verification successful! The task has been verified as authentic.")
        
        # Module 2: GIS Tracking
        print("🛰️ [GIS & SATELLITE] Tracking the location...")
        if 21.5 <= latitude <= 22.5 and 80.0 <= longitude <= 81.0:
            print("🎯 GIS Confirmation: The location is within the affected green-belt area of the MOIL/HCL mining zone.")
            self.user_wallet["earned_credits"] += 50
            print(f"🎉 Congratulations {self.user_wallet['name']}! 50 Green Credits have been added to your wallet.")
            print(f"🏢 [CSR LINKAGE] You are qualified for 1st priority in the upcoming MOIL/HCL apprenticeship batch!")
            return True
        else:
            print("❌ GIS Alert: The location is outside the mining area.")
            return False

if __name__ == "__main__":
    portal = GreenSkillsPortal()
    # Test run using the Balaghat location
    portal.simulate_submission(101, 21.8124, 80.1837)



🛠️ Technical Design Document (TDD)

1. System Introduction

This system uses geo-fencing, satellite tracking (ISRO Bhuvan GIS), and AI image detection to verify social activities carried out by rural and tribal youth, such as tree plantation and eco-furniture making, and rewards them with Green Credits.

2. Database Architecture (Database Schema Sample)

The system uses the following fields to securely store user data:

* "user_id": Unique youth identification number (MY Bharat ID)
* "gps_coordinates": Used for location verification (Latitude/Longitude)
* "green_credits_balance": Accumulated points that can be used for employment or apprenticeship priority.


🧪 Sample Data & Test Cases

Test Case 1: Successful Verification

* Input Location: Latitude 21.8124, Longitude 80.1837 (Balaghat mining area)
* Expected Result: The AI verification will pass the uploaded photo, the GIS validation will confirm that the location falls within the defined target area, and 50 Green Credit Points will be added to the user's wallet.

Test Case 2: Failed Location Verification

* Input Location: Latitude 28.6139, Longitude 77.2090 (Delhi — outside the mining area)
* Expected Result: The AI verification may pass the uploaded photo, but the GIS validation will reject the submission because the location is outside the defined target district/area.



